    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`). The audit log confirms the fiscal-year YY flowing through: `membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26` for a `2026-09-18` registration.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved every date-derived value onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July), with a single source of truth for the fiscal-year math.\n\n**New \u2014 `FiscalYear` (`rest/function/owner/FiscalYear.java`)**\nThe one definition of the fiscal year. A date on/after 1 July belongs to the fiscal year beginning that calendar year; the year is identified by its **start** year and labelled `FY<YY>` (1 Jul 2026\u201330 Jun 2027 \u2192 `FY26`). Exposes `label`/`shortYear` (public, used by the mapper) and package-private `startYear`/`between` (fiscal years elapsed).\n\n**Changed:**\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 membership number's year segment now uses `FiscalYear.shortYear(...)` instead of `registrationDate.getYear() % 100`; added a new derived `fiscalYear` field (`FiscalYear.label(...)`), mirroring how `ageBand`/`membershipNumber` are derived (not stored).\n- **`Tenure`** \u2014 now `fiscalYears(...)`, counting elapsed fiscal years via `FiscalYear.between(...)` rather than 365-day windows; keeps the null/\"unset \u21d2 zero\" tenure guard as its own concern.\n- **`MembershipPoints`** \u2014 long-tenure bonus now gates on \"over 1 fiscal year\" (`LONG_TENURE_FISCAL_YEARS`) instead of `> 365` days; parameter renamed `tenureFiscalYears`.\n- **`AssignMembershipLevel`** \u2014 calls `Tenure.fiscalYears(...)`.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` schema property (so `OwnerDto` gains the field) and updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to the fiscal-year basis.\n\n**Design note:** I labelled the fiscal year by its *starting* calendar year. This keeps `fiscalYear`, the membership number's `M<YY>`, and tenure all consistent, and means the membership number is unchanged from prior behaviour for Jul\u2013Dec registrations (only Jan\u2013Jun registrations shift down by one, which is the intended fiscal correction). The other convention (naming by the ending year) would also pass the test \u2014 flag if you'd prefer that.",
